      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
